From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/display/pvg: PVG_FIXUPS_NO_SCAN: breakpoints only, for tests

The RAM scan usually patches the Metal code before any process reaches the
breakpoint, so the breakpoint path is rarely exercised. With
PVG_FIXUPS_NO_SCAN set the scan is skipped and only breakpoints apply the
fixups (to test them, e.g. under WHPX).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/display/pvg/pvg-guest-fixups.c |    8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/pvg/pvg-guest-fixups.c b/hw/display/pvg/pvg-guest-fixups.c
index 6523778..a89b9d3 100644
--- a/hw/display/pvg/pvg-guest-fixups.c
+++ b/hw/display/pvg/pvg-guest-fixups.c
@@ -218,6 +218,7 @@ static void *fixup_thread(void *opaque)
 {
     PVGGuestFixups *f = opaque;
     int64_t last_scan = INT64_MIN / 2;
+    bool no_scan = g_getenv("PVG_FIXUPS_NO_SCAN") != NULL;
 
     rcu_register_thread();
     qemu_mutex_lock(&f->lock);
@@ -246,8 +247,11 @@ static void *fixup_thread(void *opaque)
         }
         /* either site fixes the bug (the .cold page may never be paged in once the branch is) */
         missing = !found_any && !qatomic_read(&f->bp_addr);
-        /* full scans are expensive (all of guest RAM): often until found, then rarely */
-        if (now - last_scan >= (missing ? SCAN_MISSING_MS : RESCAN_MS)) {
+        /*
+         * full scans are expensive (all of guest RAM): often until found, then rarely.
+         * PVG_FIXUPS_NO_SCAN (testing): breakpoints only.
+         */
+        if (now - last_scan >= (missing ? SCAN_MISSING_MS : RESCAN_MS) && !no_scan) {
             ScanCtx c = { .f = f };
 
             last_scan = now;
-- 
